WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.086 --> 00:00:06.679
After the fairy wind's mischief, Ellen was never left alone.

2
00:00:06.680 --> 00:00:11.106
Everyone held her tightly so she couldn't float away.

3
00:00:11.107 --> 00:00:14.231
She was tied to her bed and carriage.

4
00:00:14.232 --> 00:00:17.213
She was carried everywhere.

5
00:00:17.214 --> 00:00:21.457
Her poor parents couldn't stop worrying.

6
00:00:21.458 --> 00:00:27.877
One day the king was counting his money.

7
00:00:27.878 --> 00:00:31.534
"My gold coins have weight," he thought sadly.

8
00:00:31.535 --> 00:00:35.196
"Yet my daughter weighs nothing at all."

9
00:00:35.197 --> 00:00:38.890
A moment later the king heard someone crying.

10
00:00:38.891 --> 00:00:41.385
It was the queen.

11
00:00:41.386 --> 00:00:47.502
The king hurried to her. "What's wrong, my queen?"

12
00:00:47.503 --> 00:00:50.659
"It's our child," the queen said.

13
00:00:50.660 --> 00:00:58.496
"Ellen is so light. What if we lose her again?" She blew her nose.

14
00:00:58.497 --> 00:01:02.997
"It's a big worry," the king said glumly.

15
00:01:02.998 --> 00:01:06.296
"And what will happen when Ellen gets married and has children?

16
00:01:06.297 --> 00:01:11.554
Our kingdom will be filled with floating babies!"

17
00:01:11.555 --> 00:01:15.790
"I have an idea," the queen said slowly.

18
00:01:15.791 --> 00:01:17.759
The king smiled.

19
00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:22.360
"You always have good ideas, my queen. What is this one?"

20
00:01:22.361 --> 00:01:26.367
"You could visit your sister," she said.

21
00:01:26.368 --> 00:01:33.834
The king coughed nervously. "Visit Lady Agnes?"

22
00:01:33.835 --> 00:01:37.138
"Yes. Tell her we're sorry.

23
00:01:37.139 --> 00:01:41.670
We didn't mean to forget her invitation," the queen said.

24
00:01:41.671 --> 00:01:52.166
"And then you must beg her to remove the spell. Please, dear!"

25
00:01:52.167 --> 00:01:55.971
The king sighed and patted his wife's shoulder.

26
00:01:55.972 --> 00:02:01.812
"Dry your tears. I'll go tomorrow."

27
00:02:01.813 --> 00:02:06.505
The next morning the king went to visit Lady Agnes.

28
00:02:06.506 --> 00:02:12.136
A servant brought tea.

29
00:02:12.137 --> 00:02:16.597
"I . . . er . . . " The king fumbled with his napkin.

30
00:02:16.598 --> 00:02:18.750
"I hope you're well, Agnes.

31
00:02:18.751 --> 00:02:21.856
I came to talk to you about something important."

32
00:02:21.857 --> 00:02:27.864
Agnes narrowed her eyes. "Yes?"

33
00:02:27.865 --> 00:02:30.685
"It's the spell," the king said.

34
00:02:30.686 --> 00:02:33.793
"You were angry I forgot to invite you to the baptism.

35
00:02:33.794 --> 00:02:38.336
So you put a spell on Ellen. And now the princess is—"

36
00:02:38.337 --> 00:02:45.600
"A spell?" Agnes laughed loudly.

37
00:02:45.601 --> 00:02:52.628
"How ridiculous! As usual, you're much too impatient, brother.

38
00:02:52.629 --> 00:02:56.689
Your silly daughter will grow out of her lightness someday.

39
00:02:56.690 --> 00:03:02.916
You just need to be patient—and mend your ways."

40
00:03:02.917 --> 00:03:08.301
"Mend my ways?" the king said. "What do you mean?"

41
00:03:08.302 --> 00:03:13.306
"Work on being a better person," Agnes sneered.

42
00:03:13.307 --> 00:03:28.562
"I'll tell you where to start. Treat your older sister with more respect!"

